      "codeGaps": [
        "Four separate components (ButtonPrimary, ButtonOutline, ButtonDestructive, ButtonText) with different prop sets; the contract is one Button with a variant.",
        "No accessibilityRole=\"button\" on any variant. Only ButtonDestructive sets accessibilityState (disabled); none expose busy while loading.",
        "Pressed state is the TouchableOpacity default (0.2); the contract uses opacity.pressed (0.7).",
        "loading is part of the shared props type but ButtonDestructive and ButtonText ignore it.",
        "Icons come from two sets (AntDesign on primary and outline, Feather on destructive) and ButtonDestructive hard-codes its icon color as #FFFFFF.",
        "Disabled looks different per variant (opacity 50, faded or neutral fill, a subtle label color for text-destructive).",
        "In Plan de Vida light mode the label is white on tan (2.0:1) for primary and white on red (about 3.8:1) for destructive (waiver PDV-W6), and the outline and text labels are tan on white (waiver PDV-W1)."
      ],
